# Line endings are part of this repository's content, not a local preference.
#
# Windows sets `core.autocrlf=true` by default, and the GitHub Windows runner
# inherits it: without this file every text file is checked out with CRLF there
# while ubuntu/macOS get LF. Two concrete breakages that causes here:
#
#   * `.nvmrc` arrives as "24\r\n". `actions/setup-node` tolerates it, but the
#     manifest guard in tests/manifests/runtime-versions.test.ts asserts the file
#     is exactly one clean line — so CI failed on Windows only.
#   * `install.sh` is POSIX sh. A CRLF copy breaks at the shebang (`\r` becomes
#     part of the interpreter path) and inside every quoted string.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes to LF in the index *and* in the working tree on
# all platforms, so the checked-out bytes match the committed bytes everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit shell/manifest declarations. `text=auto` already infers these, but
# these two are the files whose breakage is silent and platform-specific, so the
# rule is stated rather than inferred.
install.sh text eol=lf
.nvmrc     text eol=lf

# If a Windows helper is ever added it must keep CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses a
# bare-LF batch file (notably `goto` labels and multi-line blocks).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted. `text=auto` would detect
# these correctly via its NUL-byte heuristic, but a heuristic misfire silently
# corrupts a committed asset, so the extensions used in this repository are
# declared outright.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.wasm  binary
